With millions of diners, 70,000+ restaurant partners and 25+ years of experience, OpenTable, part of Booking Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ: BKNG), is an industry leader with a passion for helping restaurants thrive. Our world-class technology empowers restaurants to focus on what matters most - their team, their guests, and their bottom line - while enabling diners to discover and book the perfect restaurant for every occasion.&nbsp;

Every employee at OpenTable has a tangible impact on what we do and how we do it. You’ll also be part of a global team and its portfolio of metasearch brands. Hospitality is all about taking care of others, and it defines our culture.

&nbsp;

About the Job:&nbsp;

The booking funnel is the most important moment in the diner journey - the point where intent becomes a reservation. OpenTable is looking for a Senior Product Manager to own that experience across apps (iOS and Android) and web (desktop and mobile web), from high-intent search and discovery through restaurant profile and checkout.

You'll set strategy against on-site conversion and cover yield, diagnose funnel friction with data, and ship experiences that are commercially sharp and genuinely delightful to use. This is a consumer product role that requires deep UI expertise and real technical depth: you'll work closely with engineers, designers, and data scientists on search, ranking, personalization, and checkout, and you'll be expected to debate UX, system design, and experiment design. The right candidate combines exceptional product sense and commercial instinct with the technical fluency to go deep with engineering.

&nbsp;

Responsibilities:

• Own the end-to-end conversion journey from diner intent to completed reservation, including search (list, map, and conversational), restaurant profile, checkout, and agentic booking.

• Set the vision, strategy, and roadmap for on-site conversion and booking economics, and be accountable for the outcomes

• Diagnose funnel drop-off with quantitative and qualitative insight, then ship experiments that improve conversion without degrading diner trust or booking quality

• Translate ambiguous diner problems into clear product requirements, including edge cases, instrumentation, and technical trade-offs that engineering can build against

• Partner with engineering, design, data science, and research on ranking, and personalization as conversion levers

• Navigate trade-offs between diner experience, restaurant value, and revenue, and communicate those trade-offs clearly to senior leadership

• Lead a cross-functional team to ship across web and mobile apps at global scale, including coordination with teams in other time zones&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Minimum Qualifications:

• 7+ years of product management experience owning consumer-facing B2C products (web and mobile) at scale.&nbsp;

• Proven ownership of a conversion funnel or high-intent consumer journey (for example, search-to-book, browse-to-order, or checkout), with a metric you owned and moved

• Experience with search, ranking, recommendations, or personalization as levers for conversion

• Exceptional product sense: you have shipped user-facing experiences where you owned the UI/UX, the friction, and the conversion outcome, not just the roadmap

• Technical and data fluency: you partner deeply with engineering on system design, data instrumentation, and experimentation; you can write a clear technical PRD; and you are comfortable with SQL or equivalent tools&nbsp;

• Experience developing and executing product strategy, managing a roadmap, and leading end-to-end product development, including A/B testing and post-launch optimization

• Experience leading cross-functional work with Engineering, Design, Data Science/Analytics, and Research

• Bachelor's degree in a related field, or equivalent practical experience

